00:00:00,010 --> 00:01:08,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:01:09,190 --> 00:01:14,800
[Connecting to You]

2
00:01:21,520 --> 00:01:22,470
Grandma,

3
00:01:23,289 --> 00:01:24,420
why are you still up?

4
00:01:26,250 --> 00:01:29,880
I'm studying
the community college's English course.

5
00:01:30,250 --> 00:01:31,780
Why are you still up?

6
00:01:36,330 --> 00:01:37,660
I'm getting some water.

7
00:01:42,450 --> 00:01:44,690
But it looks like there's a Diamond Sutra

8
00:01:44,690 --> 00:01:46,229
on top of

9
00:01:46,250 --> 00:01:47,770
your textbook.

10
00:01:49,190 --> 00:01:52,820
Sometimes when I get tired of
learning English,

11
00:01:52,890 --> 00:01:54,590
I chant sutras.

12
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:58,500
Do you think Jiakai

13
00:01:58,580 --> 00:02:00,340
is a bit...

14
00:02:02,970 --> 00:02:04,420
special?

15
00:02:06,390 --> 00:02:07,690
Do you mean

16
00:02:08,039 --> 00:02:09,910
he can see the threads?

17
00:02:11,050 --> 00:02:12,480
Did he tell you?

18
00:02:12,820 --> 00:02:13,480
Yes.

19
00:02:14,660 --> 00:02:15,530
That's right.

20
00:02:15,910 --> 00:02:18,500
He often gets possessed like that.

21
00:02:19,090 --> 00:02:24,140
I'm worried he can't make friends,
so I chant sutras.

22
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:26,940
It gives me peace of mind.

23
00:02:30,040 --> 00:02:30,750
Grandma,

24
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:34,130
since you're so worried about him,

25
00:02:34,720 --> 00:02:36,630
why wouldn't you want him to come back?

26
00:02:36,630 --> 00:02:39,260
How could I not want him back?

27
00:02:45,650 --> 00:02:47,280
I'm just scared.

28
00:02:47,850 --> 00:02:49,860
At my age,

29
00:02:50,850 --> 00:02:53,450
how many more years
do I have left to be with him?

30
00:02:53,540 --> 00:02:56,800
Spending the most precious time
of his life

31
00:02:56,980 --> 00:02:58,980
with an old lady like me?

32
00:02:59,450 --> 00:03:01,490
I don't want that.

33
00:03:01,930 --> 00:03:03,920
I'm not worth it.

34
00:03:10,170 --> 00:03:11,590
Actually, I...

35
00:03:12,420 --> 00:03:14,120
really envy him.

36
00:03:14,630 --> 00:03:18,120
He has a home he can always go back to
whenever he wants.

37
00:03:19,040 --> 00:03:20,590
Not everyone has that.

38
00:03:22,290 --> 00:03:23,300
What do you mean?

39
00:03:25,579 --> 00:03:27,790
There's nothing wrong with

40
00:03:28,790 --> 00:03:30,840
wanting to be with someone you love.

41
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:41,060
So...

42
00:03:42,040 --> 00:03:43,790
Do you

43
00:03:43,790 --> 00:03:46,660
like him?

44
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,210
You don't have to ask like that.

45
00:03:49,870 --> 00:03:52,620
Actually, I'm not sure.

46
00:03:54,950 --> 00:03:56,350
What about you, Grandma?

47
00:03:56,410 --> 00:03:57,600
Do you like him?

48
00:03:58,320 --> 00:04:00,720
It doesn't matter
whether I like him or not.

49
00:04:01,030 --> 00:04:02,890
I'm not the one dating him.

50
00:04:03,720 --> 00:04:04,730
That's right.

51
00:04:05,190 --> 00:04:05,920
Then...

52
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:08,780
Grandma, would you be against

53
00:04:09,540 --> 00:04:10,650
us being together?

54
00:04:11,330 --> 00:04:13,140
Why would I be against it?

55
00:04:13,630 --> 00:04:15,930
Anyone who stands in the way
of their children's happiness

56
00:04:15,930 --> 00:04:17,930
doesn't deserve to be their family.

57
00:04:18,470 --> 00:04:20,839
If you really like him,

58
00:04:20,870 --> 00:04:22,370
and he really likes you,

59
00:04:22,970 --> 00:04:24,800
just go for it.

60
00:04:26,980 --> 00:04:28,440
What are you afraid of?

61
00:04:29,900 --> 00:04:32,380
Grandma, you're so cool.

62
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:34,610
Did you think
I was just a crazy old woman?

63
00:04:34,610 --> 00:04:35,650
No.

64
00:04:45,500 --> 00:04:47,050
[The 11th Thread]

65
00:04:47,070 --> 00:04:48,070
[Zeigarnik Effect]

66
00:04:48,100 --> 00:04:50,130
[Why do people always dwell on the past?]

67
00:04:52,350 --> 00:04:53,650
[Mom] [Are you busy?]

68
00:04:53,670 --> 00:04:57,900
[Mom] [Did your dad look for you?]

69
00:05:01,960 --> 00:05:03,390
Are you done?

70
00:05:04,540 --> 00:05:06,690
Do you remember where the hair dryer is?

71
00:05:06,690 --> 00:05:07,380
Yes.

72
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:10,040
Thank you for driving me here

73
00:05:10,290 --> 00:05:13,490
and waiting at the hospital
with Grandma and me all night.

74
00:05:13,660 --> 00:05:15,160
You have dark circles now.

75
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:16,940
Do I?

76
00:05:17,320 --> 00:05:18,050
A little bit.

77
00:05:19,650 --> 00:05:23,320
Oh, and thank you for chanting the Diamond
Sutra with Grandma the other day,

78
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:25,250
even though you're such a skeptic.

79
00:05:26,700 --> 00:05:27,790
Chanting?

80
00:05:28,680 --> 00:05:29,540
Did I?

81
00:05:42,460 --> 00:05:44,190
It's not that I don’t trust you.

82
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:47,480
I just didn't know
how to talk about my own stuff,

83
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:48,880
so I didn't say anything.

84
00:05:50,510 --> 00:05:51,570
What do you mean?

85
00:05:53,920 --> 00:05:55,550
It's what we talked about

86
00:05:55,650 --> 00:05:57,320
in the park last night.

87
00:05:59,300 --> 00:06:00,360
Actually,

88
00:06:02,810 --> 00:06:04,770
I haven't seen him for a long time,

89
00:06:05,890 --> 00:06:07,690
and I don't want to see him again.

90
00:06:08,950 --> 00:06:10,120
As for my mom,

91
00:06:11,250 --> 00:06:13,010
we still keep in touch,

92
00:06:13,030 --> 00:06:14,370
but we're not close.

93
00:06:16,140 --> 00:06:17,620
I haven't gone back for the holidays

94
00:06:17,620 --> 00:06:18,730
in recent years.

95
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:22,240
That's my family's current situation.

96
00:06:25,820 --> 00:06:27,640
I know you must have your reasons

97
00:06:27,930 --> 00:06:30,060
for keeping these things to yourself.

98
00:06:30,740 --> 00:06:33,350
I was throwing a tantrum yesterday.

99
00:06:33,590 --> 00:06:34,310
I'm sorry.

100
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:37,730
I shouldn't have said those words.

101
00:06:38,170 --> 00:06:40,510
Maybe God took away your third eye

102
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:42,270
just to remind you

103
00:06:43,030 --> 00:06:45,330
not to rely on it to judge everything

104
00:06:45,630 --> 00:06:46,960
or make every decision.

105
00:06:47,080 --> 00:06:49,940
What you really need
is to communicate with people.

106
00:06:50,409 --> 00:06:51,370
God?

107
00:06:51,980 --> 00:06:54,580
Since when did you become
God's spokesperson?

108
00:06:57,420 --> 00:06:59,420
Maybe spending so much time with you

109
00:06:59,460 --> 00:07:01,390
has made me more familiar with God.

110
00:07:01,630 --> 00:07:02,630
You better be.

111
00:07:15,920 --> 00:07:17,190
Why do you have this?

112
00:07:21,020 --> 00:07:23,340
It's a shoelace.

113
00:07:29,610 --> 00:07:31,270
Why do you have this shoelace?

114
00:07:32,110 --> 00:07:34,520
A big brother gave it to me

115
00:07:34,550 --> 00:07:36,000
a long time ago.

116
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:37,980
What's wrong?

117
00:07:38,530 --> 00:07:39,900
Why are you so curious?

118
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:51,310
Because it's mine.

119
00:08:01,140 --> 00:08:02,340
Follow me. Follow me.

120
00:08:02,350 --> 00:08:03,490
Let's go.

121
00:08:05,170 --> 00:08:06,880
OK, nice! Great!

122
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:09,310
What are you doing?

123
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:11,730
Skipping class.

124
00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:14,200
I'm hiding here so I won't get caught.

125
00:08:14,200 --> 00:08:15,790
What about you? What are you doing?

126
00:08:15,790 --> 00:08:18,700
My parents' thread is missing,
and I'm looking for it.

127
00:08:18,700 --> 00:08:19,950
What thread?

128
00:08:20,130 --> 00:08:21,170
Just a thread.

129
00:08:24,680 --> 00:08:27,630
Jiakai, why are you here?

130
00:08:27,830 --> 00:08:29,360
I'm looking for something.

131
00:08:29,470 --> 00:08:30,960
Looking for something?

132
00:08:34,080 --> 00:08:36,200
You need to head over there quickly.

133
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:36,730
Okay.

134
00:08:36,760 --> 00:08:37,950
Don't forget.

135
00:08:42,860 --> 00:08:44,090
I'm leaving.

136
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:49,450
Here, take this.

137
00:08:50,240 --> 00:08:51,430
Stick it there.

138
00:08:53,450 --> 00:08:54,560
Thanks.

139
00:08:55,370 --> 00:08:56,250
By the way,

140
00:08:57,730 --> 00:08:59,840
though I don't know what thread
you're looking for,

141
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:02,180
take this as a thread.

142
00:09:02,400 --> 00:09:03,860
My phone number is on it.

143
00:09:03,890 --> 00:09:06,180
You can call me when you're bored.

144
00:09:06,870 --> 00:09:07,850
Thanks.

145
00:09:12,010 --> 00:09:12,960
Bye-bye.

146
00:09:14,140 --> 00:09:15,940
You were the one skipping class?

147
00:09:15,960 --> 00:09:19,760
Now I finally understand what thread
you were looking for back then.

148
00:09:19,830 --> 00:09:22,620
Actually, I really wanted to
call you back then.

149
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:24,730
But I accidentally threw the shoelace

150
00:09:24,730 --> 00:09:26,490
in the washing machine,

151
00:09:26,700 --> 00:09:29,070
and the words got blurred, so I gave up.

152
00:09:29,100 --> 00:09:31,760
You just carelessly tossed away
what I gave you?

153
00:09:32,070 --> 00:09:33,770
I told you it was an accident.

154
00:09:37,580 --> 00:09:40,310
It's not like you'll be
without a thread forever.

155
00:09:41,370 --> 00:09:43,430
You have the one I gave you, don't you?

156
00:09:51,460 --> 00:09:53,090
So, you kept pestering me

157
00:09:53,110 --> 00:09:54,520
about being my informant

158
00:09:54,690 --> 00:09:57,020
because I was the only one
connected to you by a thread?

159
00:09:57,020 --> 00:09:58,770
How do you even know that?

160
00:09:58,870 --> 00:09:59,700
Why?

161
00:10:03,260 --> 00:10:04,880
Now that you've lost your third eye,

162
00:10:04,880 --> 00:10:06,790
you can't see the thread between us.

163
00:10:06,790 --> 00:10:07,690
But it's okay.

164
00:10:08,430 --> 00:10:10,290
Let's use this shoelace instead.

165
00:10:11,490 --> 00:10:14,780
You don't have to worry about
not being able to find me anymore,

166
00:10:14,780 --> 00:10:16,180
because I'll come to you.

167
00:10:25,200 --> 00:10:27,380
Haven't you always been curious about

168
00:10:27,410 --> 00:10:29,400
the color of the thread between us?

169
00:10:30,260 --> 00:10:31,720
Are you willing to tell me?

170
00:10:35,710 --> 00:10:36,740
It's...

171
00:10:48,080 --> 00:10:48,960
Really?

172
00:10:54,110 --> 00:10:55,910
I'm going to buy some breakfast.

173
00:10:58,730 --> 00:11:00,990
Hey! How could you stop halfway through?

174
00:11:04,740 --> 00:11:07,600
Grandma, I cooked some food
and left it on the table.

175
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:09,080
Remember to eat.

176
00:11:10,420 --> 00:11:14,050
Do you think I'm not fat enough?

177
00:11:16,390 --> 00:11:17,670
After you go back,

178
00:11:18,140 --> 00:11:21,750
remember to eat and sleep on time.

179
00:11:21,960 --> 00:11:23,710
Don't skimp on money.

180
00:11:24,280 --> 00:11:25,460
Okay, Grandma.

181
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:26,620
You too.

182
00:11:26,640 --> 00:11:28,600
Call me if you need anything,

183
00:11:28,620 --> 00:11:29,590
and I'll come back.

184
00:11:29,590 --> 00:11:30,330
Okay.

185
00:11:32,630 --> 00:11:33,750
Dawei,

186
00:11:33,770 --> 00:11:36,150
whenever you want to come home,

187
00:11:36,250 --> 00:11:38,040
just come back.

188
00:11:42,470 --> 00:11:45,970
We take care of each other,
and that makes us family.

189
00:11:46,970 --> 00:11:48,110
Understand?

190
00:11:48,360 --> 00:11:49,360
Yes.

191
00:11:50,980 --> 00:11:51,890
Thanks, Grandma.

192
00:11:51,890 --> 00:11:52,290
Okay,

193
00:11:52,310 --> 00:11:53,860
give me a hug.

194
00:11:56,200 --> 00:11:57,720
Grandma, I want a hug too.

195
00:12:02,640 --> 00:12:05,300
[Police]

196
00:12:09,260 --> 00:12:11,530
How is it, Jiakai? Do you have a plan?

197
00:12:11,730 --> 00:12:12,690
What plan?

198
00:12:12,720 --> 00:12:14,600
A new part-time job plan?

199
00:12:14,620 --> 00:12:15,780
Of course not!

200
00:12:15,810 --> 00:12:17,270
It's Dawei's birthday.

201
00:12:17,290 --> 00:12:19,280
As his boyfriend, don't you have...

202
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:20,280
Keep it down!

203
00:12:20,620 --> 00:12:21,830
How did you know?

204
00:12:22,940 --> 00:12:24,600
Why are you so surprised?

205
00:12:25,150 --> 00:12:28,080
The way you treat each other
makes it pretty obvious.

206
00:12:28,100 --> 00:12:30,510
So, have you figured out a birthday plan?

207
00:12:30,700 --> 00:12:31,640
Not yet.

208
00:12:32,360 --> 00:12:34,520
But I prepared a jacket for him.

209
00:12:34,800 --> 00:12:35,970
Just a jacket?

210
00:12:37,190 --> 00:12:38,820
Do you have any advice?

211
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:43,750
How about going to the amusement park?

212
00:12:43,750 --> 00:12:45,000
Amusement park?

213
00:12:45,160 --> 00:12:47,330
I remember Dawei said
he'd never been to one.

214
00:12:47,330 --> 00:12:49,520
Not even for those school field trips

215
00:12:49,540 --> 00:12:50,470
when he was a kid?

216
00:12:50,610 --> 00:12:51,690
We were discussing

217
00:12:51,720 --> 00:12:53,320
what rides we were afraid of,

218
00:12:53,380 --> 00:12:55,040
and Dawei said he'd never been on any,

219
00:12:55,040 --> 00:12:57,330
because his parents never took him there
when he was a kid.

220
00:12:57,330 --> 00:12:58,580
Really?

221
00:12:58,610 --> 00:13:00,810
I think it's a good idea. Think about it.

222
00:13:00,830 --> 00:13:01,460
Bye.

223
00:13:02,860 --> 00:13:03,480
Zhiling.

224
00:13:03,510 --> 00:13:04,360
Chief.

225
00:13:04,380 --> 00:13:05,500
-Stay here.
-Okay.

226
00:13:05,530 --> 00:13:08,070
Everyone, come over here.

227
00:13:09,090 --> 00:13:10,340
Everyone,

228
00:13:10,360 --> 00:13:12,230
today is Jiakai's

229
00:13:12,260 --> 00:13:14,430
last day

230
00:13:14,510 --> 00:13:16,740
working with us.

231
00:13:16,930 --> 00:13:17,370
So,

232
00:13:17,400 --> 00:13:20,430
to thank him for his hard work
over the past two months,

233
00:13:20,450 --> 00:13:22,580
I especially wrote a character

234
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:24,270
for him.

235
00:13:24,500 --> 00:13:27,700
[Happiness]

236
00:13:25,250 --> 00:13:26,560
It's "Happiness."

237
00:13:26,580 --> 00:13:28,690
Let's wish him

238
00:13:28,710 --> 00:13:30,210
happiness forever.

239
00:13:31,360 --> 00:13:34,560
Come on, Jiakai.
Congratulations on your graduation!

240
00:13:35,870 --> 00:13:37,240
Jiakai has graduated!

241
00:13:37,270 --> 00:13:39,270
Congratulations on your graduation!

242
00:13:39,270 --> 00:13:40,390
Don't worry, everyone.

243
00:13:40,390 --> 00:13:42,220
I'll often come back to see you.

244
00:13:42,420 --> 00:13:43,480
You must come back.

245
00:13:43,570 --> 00:13:44,460
I will.

246
00:13:44,530 --> 00:13:45,590
Congratulations.

247
00:13:45,660 --> 00:13:47,070
Dawei, go take a picture.

248
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:48,690
Hurry up, it's his last day.

249
00:13:53,840 --> 00:13:54,570
Come on.

250
00:13:55,230 --> 00:13:58,690
One, two, three.

251
00:14:00,460 --> 00:14:01,670
Okay.

252
00:14:06,130 --> 00:14:07,320
Come back often.

253
00:14:07,810 --> 00:14:08,900
Of course I will.

254
00:14:09,660 --> 00:14:11,200
Don't be brought back.

255
00:14:11,250 --> 00:14:12,160
I know.

256
00:14:27,780 --> 00:14:28,960
It's on the house.

257
00:14:30,510 --> 00:14:31,510
Looks delicious.

258
00:14:39,290 --> 00:14:40,720
Are you free next Sunday?

259
00:14:43,450 --> 00:14:45,380
I'm not sure. I have to check.

260
00:14:45,560 --> 00:14:46,620
What's the matter?

261
00:14:48,430 --> 00:14:50,830
Don't tell me you forgot
your own birthday.

262
00:14:51,720 --> 00:14:52,750
Oh, right,

263
00:14:52,850 --> 00:14:54,270
it's next Sunday.

264
00:14:59,210 --> 00:15:00,540
Let me tell you a secret.

265
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:04,260
Actually,

266
00:15:05,140 --> 00:15:07,430
I never really celebrated

267
00:15:07,460 --> 00:15:08,920
my birthday growing up,

268
00:15:09,650 --> 00:15:12,650
so I never bothered to remember the date.

269
00:15:14,160 --> 00:15:16,370
You don't celebrate with friends either?

270
00:15:16,370 --> 00:15:18,810
Or maybe colleagues at the police station?

271
00:15:23,830 --> 00:15:26,720
Then do you want any gifts
for your birthday?

272
00:15:36,840 --> 00:15:37,970
What does that mean?

273
00:15:39,160 --> 00:15:40,560
I only want to be with you.

274
00:15:47,730 --> 00:15:49,930
If you're free next Sunday,

275
00:15:51,220 --> 00:15:52,950
let's go to the amusement park.

276
00:15:54,350 --> 00:15:55,680
Why the amusement park?

277
00:16:00,300 --> 00:16:01,770
The other day,

278
00:16:02,130 --> 00:16:04,820
I suddenly thought about how I used to
go to amusement parks with my family,

279
00:16:04,820 --> 00:16:06,090
and I really missed it.

280
00:16:07,310 --> 00:16:10,910
I thought it'd be nice

281
00:16:12,170 --> 00:16:13,390
if I could go with you.

282
00:16:15,430 --> 00:16:16,430
Okay.

283
00:16:16,460 --> 00:16:17,290
Really?

284
00:16:17,310 --> 00:16:18,540
